<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Statute of Westminster 1931</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1931</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Statute of Westminster</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Statute of Westminster 1931 was an Act of the British Parliament that recognised the legislative independence of the self-governing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">dominions</a>. It applied to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, Ireland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> treat it as a major step in the transition to the Commonwealth.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/statute-of-westminster-1931.jpg" alt="Statute of Westminster 1931" width="320" height="317" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_the_United_Kingdom_(1901%E2%80%931952).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
